==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|valourous}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂welh₁-|id=rule}}
From {{uder|en|fro|valeureux}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈvælərəs/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-valorous.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having or displaying [[valour]].
#* {{circa|1490}}, {{w|William Caxton}} (translator), ''The Boke of {{w|Aeneid|Eneydos}}'', Westminster, Preface,<sup>[http://name.umdl.umich.edu/A14476.0001.001]</sup>
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 5|IV|4|text={{...}} he esteems himself happy that he hath fallen into the hands of one, as he thinks, the most brave, '''valorous''', and thrice-worthy signieur of England.}}
#* {{RQ:Scott Ivanhoe|15|text={{...}} I shall be at York—at the head of my daring and '''valorous''' fellows, as ready to support any bold design as thy policy can be to form one.}}
#* {{RQ:Hemingway Farewell to Arms|page=75|passage=He held up the glass. ‘To your '''valorous''' wounds. To the silver medal. {{...}}’}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=w:Andrea Levy|title={{w|Small Island (novel)|Small Island}}|location=London|publisher=Review|chapter=12|page=139|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/smallisland00levy/page/139/mode/1up|passage=There are many '''valorous''' stories told of her, which enthral grown men as well as children.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=David Wallace-Wells|title=Bill Gates Explains His Plans to Close the Gates Foundation in 2045|date=2025-05-08|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/08/magazine/bill-gates-foundation-closing-2045.html|passage=For all its pragmatic public-health spade work, the foundation has also served as a kind of '''valorous''' abstraction — the seeming embodiment of “the Golden Rule,” in a phrase that Bill Gates likes to use, and the face of an increasingly anachronistic era of elite optimism.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260219193248/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/08/magazine/bill-gates-foundation-closing-2045.html|archivedate=19 February 2026}}

